From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:44:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] mcc-mnc: 450 is Korea (Rep. of), 467 the DPRK

The table had them the other way round: a SIM or network with MCC 450
(every South Korean operator) came out as "KP", so cellbroadcastd looked
for North Korea in the service provider database, found no channels and
fell back to its defaults. ITU-T E.212 assigns 450 to Korea (Rep. of)
and 467 to the Democratic People's Republic of Korea.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 src/gm-mcc-mnc.c     | 4 ++--
 tests/test-mcc-mnc.c | 9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gm-mcc-mnc.c b/src/gm-mcc-mnc.c
index 0c33128..f592755 100644
--- a/src/gm-mcc-mnc.c
+++ b/src/gm-mcc-mnc.c
@@ -146,7 +146,7 @@ struct mcc_list mcc_list[] = {
   {438, "TM"},
   {440, "JP"},
   {441, "JP"},
-  {450, "KP"},
+  {450, "KR"},
   {452, "VN"},
   {454, "HK"},
   {455, "MO"},
@@ -155,7 +155,7 @@ struct mcc_list mcc_list[] = {
   {460, "CN"},
   {461, "CN"},
   {466, "TW"},
-  {467, "KR"},
+  {467, "KP"},
   {470, "BD"},
   {472, "MV"},
   {502, "MY"},
diff --git a/tests/test-mcc-mnc.c b/tests/test-mcc-mnc.c
index 78456a3..4927113 100644
--- a/tests/test-mcc-mnc.c
+++ b/tests/test-mcc-mnc.c
@@ -21,6 +21,15 @@ test_country_code (void)
   g_assert_no_error (err);
   g_assert_cmpstr (country_code, ==, "CH");
 
+  /* ITU-T E.212: 450 is Korea (Rep. of), 467 is the Democratic People's Rep. of Korea */
+  country_code = gm_mcc_to_iso ("45006", &err);
+  g_assert_no_error (err);
+  g_assert_cmpstr (country_code, ==, "KR");
+
+  country_code = gm_mcc_to_iso ("467", &err);
+  g_assert_no_error (err);
+  g_assert_cmpstr (country_code, ==, "KP");
+
   country_code = gm_mcc_to_iso ("", &err);
   g_assert_null (country_code);
   g_assert_error (err, GM_ERROR, G_IO_ERROR_NOT_FOUND);
-- 
2.56.0

